@Eliaquim
Cool! But doesn't that also have the problem that if more than 1 character level up and get a skill at the same time.
EDIT: Though can be solved by making the choices for each dude in the loop I guess

@Eliaquim
Well, reporting with good news and bad news! The good news, the event runs! It detects when a new skill is being added and procs the choice menu...
The bad news is that it doesn't actually delete the skill... or move on to another Actor. It just repeats the same set of names and variables as many times as Actors have gained skills.

@Eliaquim
This is what I have! I did notice the typos and the > 3, so don't worry about them!
It works pretty well, but what ends up happening is that for some reason, it runs twice. First time it runs okay, displays the message X forgot the move... and then it prompts to choose which move to forget once more before ending. And if more than 1 Actors gain skills, the second loop has the skills of the next Actor but still displays the first actor's name, the third loop has the the second Actor's name and skills, and then it repeats that once more before it finishes.
